.TH "mktmp" "1" "July 2026" "BetterScripts mktmp v1.0.0" "mktemp replacement written entirely in POSIX.1."
.hy
.SS MKTMP
.SS SYNOPSIS
.IP
.nf
\f[C]
mktmp <ARGUMENT>...
\f[R]
.fi
.SS DESCRIPTION
.PP
The command `mktmp' is a wrapper for functionality provided by
`libpath.sh', offering a portable, POSIX-compliant alternative to
`mktemp(1)'.
.PP
Documentation for \f[V]libpath.sh\f[R] applies (and is not replicated
here).
